iPad: more room around the D-pad and ABXY

On an iPad, the default landscape layout puts the shoulder buttons
right on top of the D-pad and ABXY clusters and L3/R3 and back/start
right next to them, so thumbs easily hit the wrong button.

On iPad only: 40 instead of 20 points between the shoulder buttons and
the clusters, and 40 points more between the centre buttons and the
clusters. The phone layouts are unchanged.

Upstream: not submitted.

